  "presentation_summary": [
    "72-year-old woman from rural Portugal had months of fatigue, asthenia, and about 5% unintentional weight loss over six months.",
    "During the month before evaluation she had irregular afternoon fever up to 38.9 degC responsive to acetaminophen.",
    "Exam showed cachexia, pale mucosa, and palpable splenomegaly 3 cm below the costal margin; ultrasound spleen length was 16 cm.",
    "Initial labs showed pancytopenia, ESR 80 mm/h, ferritin 1282 ng/mL, creatinine 1.55 mg/dL, mild cytocolestatic liver injury, albumin 2.4 g/dL, CRP 1.17 mg/dL, and polyclonal hypergammaglobulinemia on serum protein electrophoresis.",
    "Bone marrow aspirate did not show parasites, but leishmaniasis serology was positive; liposomal amphotericin B was started and the patient later died after urinary septic shock."
  ],
